r services consist of customer services and administrative support services, as well as information technology services. The company was incorporated in 1925 and is based in Erie, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian William Bolash Esq. | Interim President & CEO | Age 59 | Compensation: $849,194 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $610K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $86K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Erie Indemnity Company is a large-cap financial services business with a $14.2B market cap on $4.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 19-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $571M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 45% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 42% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.41679684949636764},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low rei